The single-pass readiness builder can report output integrity as ready while silently masking missing symbol/timeframe coverage due duplicate prediction rows, which undermines the proof-first evidence contract. This is a correctness issue in the readiness artifact itself, so the patch should not be considered correct.

Review comment:

- [P2] Reject duplicate rows when validating CUDA prediction grid — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/backend/app/services/live_gate/single_pass.py:414-420
  `build_output_integrity_status()` marks output integrity as READY based only on `violations`, while `complete_grid` is a passive field. Because missing coverage is detected via `missing_grid_count` computed from total row count, a missing `(symbol, timeframe)` pair can be hidden by a duplicate row (so `len(rows)` still equals `expected_count`), yielding `status: CUDA_TRAINER_OUTPUT_INTEGRITY_READY` even though coverage is incomplete. That contradicts the “missing rows are explicit evidence” requirement and can produce a false positive when evaluating readiness.
